WEBVTT

00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.321
One tulip bulb:

00:00:01.331 --> 00:00:02.869
10,000 guilders.

00:00:02.969 --> 00:00:04.356
That was the peak price of the

00:00:04.366 --> 00:00:07.755
Semper Augustus, in Holland's tulip mania.

00:00:07.765 --> 00:00:10.063
At the peak, rare bulbs cost several

00:00:10.073 --> 00:00:12.091
times a worker's yearly pay.

00:00:12.101 --> 00:00:14.431
And the prized flame-like streaks?

00:00:14.441 --> 00:00:15.994
They came from a virus that made

00:00:16.004 --> 00:00:17.293
the bulbs sickly.

00:00:17.303 --> 00:00:21.715
Then, in February 1637,
prices suddenly collapsed.

00:00:21.815 --> 00:00:24.088
The famous story says many investors were

00:00:24.098 --> 00:00:27.713
ruined and Dutch trade was badly shaken.

00:00:27.723 --> 00:00:29.622
But how many really went bust?

00:00:29.632 --> 00:00:32.791
Historian Anne Goldgar went
through the archives,

00:00:32.801 --> 00:00:34.641
and she couldn't find anybody who went

00:00:34.651 --> 00:00:35.776
bankrupt.
